      "When the Palace Cinema announced that it would close, most residents assumed the building would become another supermarket. The cinema had served the town for nearly ninety years, but rising costs and declining audiences had made it difficult for the private owner to continue. [GAP 1]",
      "The group quickly discovered that affection for the building was not the same as a workable business plan. Volunteers surveyed residents, spoke to independent cinema managers and calculated how many tickets would need to be sold each week. [GAP 2] This evidence persuaded the local council to delay permission for a change of use.",
