      "After reopening, the Palace did not try to compete directly with large entertainment centres. It showed a mixture of recent films, classics and documentaries, and invited local groups to suggest events. [GAP 4] A popular monthly programme now pairs a film with a discussion led by someone who works in the subject area.",
      "The project still faces difficult decisions. Energy bills are high, specialist repairs are expensive and volunteers cannot cover every shift. [GAP 5] The cinema therefore employs a small professional team while using volunteers for events and community activities.",
      "Its survival offers a lesson that extends beyond one building. A community campaign needs enthusiasm, but it also needs research, transparent finances and a reason for people to return after the celebration is over. [GAP 6] In the Palace's case, saving the past worked because the organisers created a useful place for the present.",
